            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="LAN03" sex="2">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName>Countess</roleName>
                        <forename>Jane Isabella</forename>
                        <surname>Butler</surname>
                        <addName>Lanesborough</addName>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1737">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1828"/>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
    'In the pursuit of well-born clients <persName key="KIN01">John King</persName> entertained lavishly and frequently. In cultivating these contacts his long-term liaison with Jane Isabella Butler, the widowed
    countess of Lanesborough (1737–1828), was of great assistance. They met in 1783 and a year later King divorced his wife before a rabbinical court in Leghorn, Italy,
    where he had fled to escape imprisonment. Although they lived as husband and wife for forty years it does not appear that they married.' (<title>DNB</title> entry on 'Jew' King).
  
</note>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
